    "readme_description": "Given an array of strings `words`, return the first **palindromic** string in the array. If there is no such string, return an **empty string** `\"\"`.\n\nA string is **palindromic** if it reads the same forward and backward.",
    "_readme_examples": {
        "list": [
            {
                "content": "```\nInput: words = [\"abc\",\"car\",\"ada\",\"racecar\",\"cool\"]\nOutput: \"ada\"\n```\n**Explanation:** The first string that is palindromic is \"ada\". Note that \"racecar\" is also palindromic, but it is not the first."
            },
            {
                "content": "```\nInput: words = [\"notapalindrome\",\"racecar\"]\nOutput: \"racecar\"\n```\n**Explanation:** The first and only string that is palindromic is \"racecar\"."
            },
            {
                "content": "```\nInput: words = [\"def\",\"ghi\"]\nOutput: \"\"\n```\n**Explanation:** There are no palindromic strings, so the empty string is returned."
